{"obs_mqv8pbng_4bdbe1713b3f":{"observation":{"hookType":"session_updated","id":"obs_mqv8pbng_4bdbe1713b3f","raw":{"additions":null,"deletions":null,"files":null,"parentID":"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI","title":"Fix vision_encoder + voice_daemon (@languages/python-pro subagent)"},"sessionId":"ses_0fae5f4c6ffe5Qb4Qcn1q8ughu","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:03:40.731Z"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8pbnk_09c9ee37a82c":{"observation":{"hookType":"prompt_submit","id":"obs_mqv8pbnk_09c9ee37a82c","raw":{"agent":"languages/python-pro","files":[],"model":{"modelID":"big-pickle","providerID":"opencode"},"parts_summary":["text"],"prompt":"Fix 3 bugs in the xnch perception module.\n\n**Bug 1: /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/perception/vision_encoder.py**\nRead the file first.\n- Line 42: `moondream.Image.open(image_bytes)` — moondream does NOT expose PIL.Image as `moondream.Image`. Fix:\n```python\ndef _encode():\n    from PIL import Image as PILImage\n    import io\n    image = PILImage.open(io.BytesIO(image_bytes))\n    return self._model.caption(image)[\"caption\"]\n```\n- Line 43: `self._model.generate(image)` — moondream's vlm API doesn't have `generate()`. The correct method is `.caption(image)` which returns `{\"caption\": str}`. Already covered by the fix above.\n\n**Bug 2: /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/perception/voice_daemon.py**\nRead the file first.\n- Line 86: `np.frombuffer(raw, dtype=np.float32).astype(np.float32)` — Microphone audio is PCM int16 (16-bit signed integers). Reinterpreting raw bytes as float32 without conversion produces garbage. Fix:\n```python\naudio_np = np.frombuffer(raw, dtype=np.int16).astype(np.float32) / 32768.0\n```\n- Line 90 (Low): Whisper auto-detects language on every call, adding ~100ms overhead. Add `language=\"en\"` parameter to the transcribe call (or make it configurable).\n\nReturn a summary of every change (file, line, what changed).","variant":null},"sessionId":"ses_0fae5f4c6ffe5Qb4Qcn1q8ughu","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:03:40.733Z","userPrompt":"Fix 3 bugs in the xnch perception module.\n\n**Bug 1: /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/perception/vision_encoder.py**\nRead the file first.\n- Line 42: `moondream.Image.open(image_bytes)` — moondream does NOT expose PIL.Image as `moondream.Image`. Fix:\n```python\ndef _encode():\n    from PIL import Image as PILImage\n    import io\n    image = PILImage.open(io.BytesIO(image_bytes))\n    return self._model.caption(image)[\"caption\"]\n```\n- Line 43: `self._model.generate(image)` — moondream's vlm API doesn't have `generate()`. The correct method is `.caption(image)` which returns `{\"caption\": str}`. Already covered by the fix above.\n\n**Bug 2: /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/perception/voice_daemon.py**\nRead the file first.\n- Line 86: `np.frombuffer(raw, dtype=np.float32).astype(np.float32)` — Microphone audio is PCM int16 (16-bit signed integers). Reinterpreting raw bytes as float32 without conversion produces garbage. Fix:\n```python\naudio_np = np.frombuffer(raw, dtype=np.int16).astype(np.float32) / 32768.0\n```\n- Line 90 (Low): Whisper auto-detects language on every call, adding ~100ms overhead. Add `language=\"en\"` parameter to the transcribe call (or make it configurable).\n\nReturn a summary of every change (file, line, what changed)."},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8pbny_b38f440c197d":{"observation":{"hookType":"session_status","id":"obs_mqv8pbny_b38f440c197d","raw":{"attempt":null,"message":"","status_type":"busy"},"sessionId":"ses_0fae5f4c6ffe5Qb4Qcn1q8ughu","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:03:40.749Z"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8pbny_777522056eb3":{"observation":{"hookType":"assistant_message","id":"obs_mqv8pbny_777522056eb3","raw":{"cost":0,"duration_ms":null,"error":null,"finish":null,"messageID":"msg_f051a0b4d002LgDIbRV4GRyjS6","mode":"languages/python-pro","modelID":"big-pickle","parentID":"msg_f051a0b3c002xYRnac8f4z27UI","providerID":"opencode","tokens":{"cache_read":0,"cache_write":0,"input":0,"output":0,"reasoning":0}},"sessionId":"ses_0fae5f4c6ffe5Qb4Qcn1q8ughu","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:03:40.750Z"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8pbra_d0c5469ccec2":{"observation":{"hookType":"session_diff","id":"obs_mqv8pbra_d0c5469ccec2","raw":{"additions":0,"deletions":0,"diffs":[],"files":[]},"sessionId":"ses_0fae5f4c6ffe5Qb4Qcn1q8ughu","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:03:40.869Z"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8pbru_2c029328902a":{"observation":{"hookType":"llm_params","id":"obs_mqv8pbru_2c029328902a","raw":{"agent":"languages/python-pro","context_limit":200000,"cost_1k_input":0,"cost_1k_output":0,"max_output_tokens":32000,"model":"opencode/big-pickle","provider_url":"https://opencode.ai/zen/v1"},"sessionId":"ses_0fae5f4c6ffe5Qb4Qcn1q8ughu","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:03:40.889Z"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8pdt7_8af93d5274c4":{"observation":{"hookType":"reasoning","id":"obs_mqv8pdt7_8af93d5274c4","raw":{"messageID":"msg_f051a0b4d002LgDIbRV4GRyjS6","text":""},"sessionId":"ses_0fae5f4c6ffe5Qb4Qcn1q8ughu","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:03:43.529Z"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8pekt_908721a41475":{"observation":{"hookType":"post_tool_use","id":"obs_mqv8pekt_908721a41475","raw":{"attachments":[],"call_id":"call_00_XLseY2krLXU18CBA6hCZ2899","duration_ms":5,"metadata":{"loaded":[],"preview":"import asyncio\nimport json\nimport time\nimport uuid\nfrom typing import Any\n\nimport redis.asyncio as aioredis\n\nfrom ..config import settings\n\n\nclass VisionEncoder:\n    def __init__(self, redis_url: str | None = None) -> None:\n        self._redis = aioredis.from_url(\n            redis_url or settings.redis_url,\n            decode_responses=True,\n        )\n        self._model = None\n        self._model_lock = asyncio.Lock()\n","truncated":false},"title":"xnch/xnch/perception/vision_encoder.py","tool_input":"{\"filePath\":\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/perception/vision_encoder.py\"}","tool_name":"read","tool_output":"<path>/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/perception/vision_encoder.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: import asyncio\n2: import json\n3: import time\n4: import uuid\n5: from typing import Any\n6: \n7: import redis.asyncio as aioredis\n8: \n9: from ..config import settings\n10: \n11: \n12: class VisionEncoder:\n13:     def __init__(self, redis_url: str | None = None) -> None:\n14:         self._redis = aioredis.from_url(\n15:             redis_url or settings.redis_url,\n16:             decode_responses=True,\n17:         )\n18:         self._model = None\n19:         self._model_lock = asyncio.Lock()\n20: \n21:     async def aclose(self) -> None:\n22:         await self._redis.aclose()\n23: \n24:     async def load_model(self) -> None:\n25:         async with self._model_lock:\n26:             if self._model is not None:\n27:                 return\n28: \n29:             def _load():\n30:                 import moondream\n31:                 return moondream.vl(model_id=\"moondream2\")\n32: \n33:             loop = asyncio.get_running_loop()\n34:             self._model = await loop.run_in_executor(None, _load)\n35: \n36:     async def encode_screenshot(self, image_bytes: bytes) -> dict[str, Any]:\n37:         await self.load_model()\n38:         loop = asyncio.get_running_loop()\n39: \n40:         def _encode():\n41:             import moondream\n42:             image = moondream.Image.open(image_bytes)\n43:             return self._model.generate(image)\n44: \n45:         description = await loop.run_in_executor(None, _encode)\n46:         perception_id = str(uuid.uuid4())\n47:         payload = {\n48:             \"id\": perception_id,\n49:             \"description\": description,\n50:             \"timestamp\": time.time(),\n51:             \"type\": \"vision\",\n52:         }\n53:         await self._redis.setex(\n54:             f\"perception:vision:{perception_id}\",\n55:             60,\n56:             json.dumps(payload),\n57:         )\n58:         return payload\n\n(End of file - total 58 lines)\n</content>"},"sessionId":"ses_0fae5f4c6ffe5Qb4Qcn1q8ughu","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:03:44.524Z","toolInput":"{\"filePath\":\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/perception/vision_encoder.py\"}","toolName":"read","toolOutput":"<path>/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/perception/vision_encoder.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: import asyncio\n2: import json\n3: import time\n4: import uuid\n5: from typing import Any\n6: \n7: import redis.asyncio as aioredis\n8: \n9: from ..config import settings\n10: \n11: \n12: class VisionEncoder:\n13:     def __init__(self, redis_url: str | None = None) -> None:\n14:         self._redis = aioredis.from_url(\n15:             redis_url or settings.redis_url,\n16:             decode_responses=True,\n17:         )\n18:         self._model = None\n19:         self._model_lock = asyncio.Lock()\n20: \n21:     async def aclose(self) -> None:\n22:         await self._redis.aclose()\n23: \n24:     async def load_model(self) -> None:\n25:         async with self._model_lock:\n26:             if self._model is not None:\n27:                 return\n28: \n29:             def _load():\n30:                 import moondream\n31:                 return moondream.vl(model_id=\"moondream2\")\n32: \n33:             loop = asyncio.get_running_loop()\n34:             self._model = await loop.run_in_executor(None, _load)\n35: \n36:     async def encode_screenshot(self, image_bytes: bytes) -> dict[str, Any]:\n37:         await self.load_model()\n38:         loop = asyncio.get_running_loop()\n39: \n40:         def _encode():\n41:             import moondream\n42:             image = moondream.Image.open(image_bytes)\n43:             return self._model.generate(image)\n44: \n45:         description = await loop.run_in_executor(None, _encode)\n46:         perception_id = str(uuid.uuid4())\n47:         payload = {\n48:             \"id\": perception_id,\n49:             \"description\": description,\n50:             \"timestamp\": time.time(),\n51:             \"type\": \"vision\",\n52:         }\n53:         await self._redis.setex(\n54:             f\"perception:vision:{perception_id}\",\n55:             60,\n56:             json.dumps(payload),\n57:         )\n58:         return payload\n\n(End of file - total 58 lines)\n</content>"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8pepd_e2153d99de2c":{"observation":{"hookType":"post_tool_use","id":"obs_mqv8pepd_e2153d99de2c","raw":{"attachments":[],"call_id":"call_01_lje7NaKaLnMoCepK9uqp7697","duration_ms":4,"metadata":{"loaded":[],"preview":"import asyncio\nimport json\nimport time\nimport uuid\nfrom typing import Any\n\nimport redis.asyncio as aioredis\n\nfrom ..config import settings\n\n\nclass VoiceDaemon:\n    def __init__(self, redis_url: str | None = None) -> None:\n        self._redis = aioredis.from_url(\n            redis_url or settings.redis_url,\n            decode_responses=True,\n        )\n        self._vad_model = None\n        self._whisper_model = None\n        self._recording = False","truncated":false},"title":"xnch/xnch/perception/voice_daemon.py","tool_input":"{\"filePath\":\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/perception/voice_daemon.py\"}","tool_name":"read","tool_output":"<path>/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/perception/voice_daemon.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: import asyncio\n2: import json\n3: import time\n4: import uuid\n5: from typing import Any\n6: \n7: import redis.asyncio as aioredis\n8: \n9: from ..config import settings\n10: \n11: \n12: class VoiceDaemon:\n13:     def __init__(self, redis_url: str | None = None) -> None:\n14:         self._redis = aioredis.from_url(\n15:             redis_url or settings.redis_url,\n16:             decode_responses=True,\n17:         )\n18:         self._vad_model = None\n19:         self._whisper_model = None\n20:         self._recording = False\n21:         self._audio_buffer: list[bytes] = []\n22: \n23:     async def aclose(self) -> None:\n24:         await self._redis.aclose()\n25: \n26:     async def load_models(self) -> None:\n27:         loop = asyncio.get_running_loop()\n28: \n29:         def _load_vad():\n30:             import silero_vad\n31:             return silero_vad.load_silero_vad()\n32: \n33:         def _load_whisper():\n34:             from faster_whisper import WhisperModel\n35:             return WhisperModel(\n36:                 \"base\",\n37:                 device=\"cuda\",\n38:                 compute_type=\"float16\",\n39:                 num_workers=1,\n40:             )\n41: \n42:         self._vad_model = await loop.run_in_executor(None, _load_vad)\n43:         self._whisper_model = await loop.run_in_executor(None, _load_whisper)\n44: \n45:     async def start_recording(self) -> dict[str, Any]:\n46:         if self._recording:\n47:             return {\"status\": \"already_recording\"}\n48:         self._recording = True\n49:         self._audio_buffer = []\n50:         return {\"status\": \"recording_started\", \"session_id\": str(uuid.uuid4())}\n51: \n52:     async def stop_recording(self) -> dict[str, Any]:\n53:         if not self._recording:\n54:             return {\"status\": \"not_recording\"}\n55:         self._recording = False\n56:         transcript = await self._transcribe()\n57:         perception_id = str(uuid.uuid4())\n58:         payload = {\n59:             \"id\": perception_id,\n60:             \"transcript\": transcript,\n61:             \"timestamp\": time.time(),\n62:             \"type\": \"voice\",\n63:         }\n64:         await self._redis.setex(\n65:             f\"perception:voice:{perception_id}\",\n66:             60,\n67:             json.dumps(payload),\n68:         )\n69:         self._audio_buffer = []\n70:         return {\n71:             \"status\": \"stopped\",\n72:             \"perception_id\": perception_id,\n73:             \"transcript\": transcript,\n74:         }\n75: \n76:     async def push_audio(self, chunk: bytes) -> None:\n77:         if not self._recording:\n78:             return\n79:         self._audio_buffer.append(chunk)\n80: \n81:     async def _transcribe(self) -> str:\n82:         if self._whisper_model is None or not self._audio_buffer:\n83:             return \"\"\n84:         import numpy as np\n85:         raw = b\"\".join(self._audio_buffer)\n86:         audio_np = np.frombuffer(raw, dtype=np.int16).astype(np.float32) / 32768.0\n87:         loop = asyncio.get_running_loop()\n88: \n89:         def _run():\n90:             segments, _ = self._whisper_model.transcribe(audio_np, beam_size=1, language=\"en\")\n91:             return \" \".join(seg.text for seg in segments).strip()\n92: \n93:         return await loop.run_in_executor(None, _run)\n94: \n95:     async def detect_silence(self, chunk: bytes, sample_rate: int = 16000) -> bool:\n96:         if self._vad_model is None:\n97:             return True\n98:         import numpy as np\n99:         audio_int16 = np.frombuffer(chunk, dtype=np.int16).astype(np.float32) / 32768.0\n100:         loop = asyncio.get_running_loop()\n101: \n102:         def _check():\n103:             return self._vad_model.is_speech(audio_int16, sample_rate)\n104: \n105:         return not await loop.run_in_executor(None, _check)\n\n(End of file - total 105 lines)\n</content>"},"sessionId":"ses_0fae5f4c6ffe5Qb4Qcn1q8ughu","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:03:44.687Z","toolInput":"{\"filePath\":\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/perception/voice_daemon.py\"}","toolName":"read","toolOutput":"<path>/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/perception/voice_daemon.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: import asyncio\n2: import json\n3: import time\n4: import uuid\n5: from typing import Any\n6: \n7: import redis.asyncio as aioredis\n8: \n9: from ..config import settings\n10: \n11: \n12: class VoiceDaemon:\n13:     def __init__(self, redis_url: str | None = None) -> None:\n14:         self._redis = aioredis.from_url(\n15:             redis_url or settings.redis_url,\n16:             decode_responses=True,\n17:         )\n18:         self._vad_model = None\n19:         self._whisper_model = None\n20:         self._recording = False\n21:         self._audio_buffer: list[bytes] = []\n22: \n23:     async def aclose(self) -> None:\n24:         await self._redis.aclose()\n25: \n26:     async def load_models(self) -> None:\n27:         loop = asyncio.get_running_loop()\n28: \n29:         def _load_vad():\n30:             import silero_vad\n31:             return silero_vad.load_silero_vad()\n32: \n33:         def _load_whisper():\n34:             from faster_whisper import WhisperModel\n35:             return WhisperModel(\n36:                 \"base\",\n37:                 device=\"cuda\",\n38:                 compute_type=\"float16\",\n39:                 num_workers=1,\n40:             )\n41: \n42:         self._vad_model = await loop.run_in_executor(None, _load_vad)\n43:         self._whisper_model = await loop.run_in_executor(None, _load_whisper)\n44: \n45:     async def start_recording(self) -> dict[str, Any]:\n46:         if self._recording:\n47:             return {\"status\": \"already_recording\"}\n48:         self._recording = True\n49:         self._audio_buffer = []\n50:         return {\"status\": \"recording_started\", \"session_id\": str(uuid.uuid4())}\n51: \n52:     async def stop_recording(self) -> dict[str, Any]:\n53:         if not self._recording:\n54:             return {\"status\": \"not_recording\"}\n55:         self._recording = False\n56:         transcript = await self._transcribe()\n57:         perception_id = str(uuid.uuid4())\n58:         payload = {\n59:             \"id\": perception_id,\n60:             \"transcript\": transcript,\n61:             \"timestamp\": time.time(),\n62:             \"type\": \"voice\",\n63:         }\n64:         await self._redis.setex(\n65:             f\"perception:voice:{perception_id}\",\n66:             60,\n67:             json.dumps(payload),\n68:         )\n69:         self._audio_buffer = []\n70:         return {\n71:             \"status\": \"stopped\",\n72:             \"perception_id\": perception_id,\n73:             \"transcript\": transcript,\n74:         }\n75: \n76:     async def push_audio(self, chunk: bytes) -> None:\n77:         if not self._recording:\n78:             return\n79:         self._audio_buffer.append(chunk)\n80: \n81:     async def _transcribe(self) -> str:\n82:         if self._whisper_model is None or not self._audio_buffer:\n83:             return \"\"\n84:         import numpy as np\n85:         raw = b\"\".join(self._audio_buffer)\n86:         audio_np = np.frombuffer(raw, dtype=np.int16).astype(np.float32) / 32768.0\n87:         loop = asyncio.get_running_loop()\n88: \n89:         def _run():\n90:             segments, _ = self._whisper_model.transcribe(audio_np, beam_size=1, language=\"en\")\n91:             return \" \".join(seg.text for seg in segments).strip()\n92: \n93:         return await loop.run_in_executor(None, _run)\n94: \n95:     async def detect_silence(self, chunk: bytes, sample_rate: int = 16000) -> bool:\n96:         if self._vad_model is None:\n97:             return True\n98:         import numpy as np\n99:         audio_int16 = np.frombuffer(chunk, dtype=np.int16).astype(np.float32) / 32768.0\n100:         loop = asyncio.get_running_loop()\n101: \n102:         def _check():\n103:             return self._vad_model.is_speech(audio_int16, sample_rate)\n104: \n105:         return not await loop.run_in_executor(None, _check)\n\n(End of file - total 105 lines)\n</content>"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8petv_6894a9f8a184":{"observation":{"hookType":"step_finish","id":"obs_mqv8petv_6894a9f8a184","raw":{"cost":0,"input_tokens":31095,"messageID":"msg_f051a0b4d002LgDIbRV4GRyjS6","output_tokens":117,"reason":"tool-calls","reasoning_tokens":37},"sessionId":"ses_0fae5f4c6ffe5Qb4Qcn1q8ughu","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:03:44.850Z"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8pevd_973b355e24aa":{"observation":{"hookType":"patch_applied","id":"obs_mqv8pevd_973b355e24aa","raw":{"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/data/stream_store/stream%3Amem-live%3Ases_0fae5f4c6ffe5Qb4Qcn1q8ughu.bin","/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/data/stream_store/stream%3Amem-live%3Ases_0fae60061ffewNVfdg0kVd2yhG.bin"],"hash":"ffb093bd7b3bcb4fcd6bd31a50e09694fa1304cc","messageID":"msg_f051a0b4d002LgDIbRV4GRyjS6"},"sessionId":"ses_0fae5f4c6ffe5Qb4Qcn1q8ughu","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:03:44.903Z"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8q0v7_8182bf60e179":{"observation":{"concepts":["image processing","PIL","vision encoder","model inference refactoring"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["Replaced moondream.Image.open with PIL.Image.open using io.BytesIO","Changed model inference call from self._model.generate(image) to self._model.caption(image)[\"caption\"]"],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/perception/vision_encoder.py"],"id":"obs_mqv8q0v7_8182bf60e179","importance":5,"narrative":"The image decoding logic was updated to use standard PIL instead of the moondream-specific Image class. The model generation call was also updated to use the 'caption' method and extract the specific caption string from the returned dictionary.","sessionId":"ses_0fae5f4c6ffe5Qb4Qcn1q8ughu","subtitle":"Updated encoding logic in vision_encoder.py to use PIL and correct model method","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:04:13.409Z","title":"Refactor vision encoder image processing and model inference","type":"file_edit"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv8q5bw_a7d411127554":{"observation":{"concepts":["audio transcription","asyncio executor","Whisper model inference","numpy audio normalization"],"confidence":1,"facts":["_transcribe method uses Whisper model for audio-to-text conversion","Audio buffer is converted from int16 to float32 normalized format","Transcription is executed in a separate thread using loop.run_in_executor to avoid blocking the event loop"],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/perception/voice_daemon.py"],"id":"obs_mqv8q5bw_a7d411127554","importance":3,"narrative":"The agent inspected the implementation of the _transcribe method in voice_daemon.py. This reveals how audio processing and model inference are handled asynchronously.","sessionId":"ses_0fae5f4c6ffe5Qb4Qcn1q8ughu","subtitle":"Inspecting _transcribe implementation in perception module","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:04:19.192Z","title":"Read voice_daemon.py transcription logic","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"}}␀�\␀Ԩ��